        "title": "Binomial Coefficients and Identities",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The binomial coefficient is the most important number in combinatorics. Three\nequivalent faces — an algebraic formula, the coefficients of `(1+x)^n`, and the\nentries of Pascal's triangle — generate a web of identities, each of which\nadmits a **bijective or combinatorial proof** (count one set two ways). The\nmultinomial coefficient is the multivariable lift."
    },
