        "section": "combinatorics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Binomial Coefficients and Identities",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The **combinatorial definition** (number of k-subsets) is primary — it makes\nidentities *visible*. The factorial formula is for computation. The generating\nidentity `(1+x)^n = Σ_k C(n,k) x^k` ports every identity into algebra and is the\ngateway to `03-GENERATING-FUNCTIONS.md`."
    },
    {
      "id": "02-BINOMIAL-AND-IDENTITIES.md#008",
      "path": [
        "02-BINOMIAL-AND-IDENTITIES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:combinatorics:02-binomial-and-identities, git-history:combinatorics:02-binomial-and-identities]",
        "canonical_path": "combinatorics/02-BINOMIAL-AND-IDENTITIES.md",
