        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "combinatorics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[binomial coefficients]",
        "section": "combinatorics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Binomial Coefficients and Identities",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Extend to **real/complex upper index** via the falling-factorial form\n`C(α,k) = α(α-1)···(α-k+1)/k!`, valid for any α — this is what powers Newton's\n**generalized binomial series** `(1+x)^α = Σ_k C(α,k) x^k` for `|x|<1`, the\nsource of `(1-x)^{-1} = Σ x^k`, `(1-4x)^{-1/2}` (Catalan), and friends."
    }
